@startuml
title Photo/video comments and rejection notifications
start
:Active user opens a feed photo or video;
:API verifies current account, feed flag
and configured feed scope (image or video);
:Validate text (1..1000 characters)
and request UUID;
:Transaction locks author row;
if (Same request already stored?) then (yes)
  :Return original result if payload matches;
else (no)
  :Enforce 5 submissions per 60 seconds;
  :Store comment as pending;
endif
:Author sees neutral confirmation
and own comment in "Meus comentários";
:Active admin reviews a photo/video comment
under /adm/comentarios;
:API checks current admin role,
comment_moderation flag and media scope;
if (Reject?) then (yes)
  :Require nonblank reason (1..500);
  :Refuse already rejected comment;
endif
:Begin transaction;
if (Conditional update matches expected version?) then (yes)
  :Store decision, moderator, review time
and increment version;
  if (Rejection?) then (yes)
    :Store reason and private notification snapshot;
  else (no)
    :Clear rejection reason;
  endif
  :Commit;
else (no)
  :Rollback and return 409;
  stop
endif
:Only approved comments appear publicly;
if (Rejected?) then (yes)
  :Request email after commit in background;
  if (email_feed_photo_comment_rejected on?) then (yes)
    :Shared EmailService sends reason to eligible author;
  else (no)
    :Skip email; keep in-app notification;
  endif
  :Author sees reason in own comment
and bell (mobile and desktop);
  :Author opens notice and selects "Entendi";
  :Persist first read timestamp scoped to recipient;
endif
stop
note right
  Public reads obey media/page visibility.
  Private reasons never enter public DTOs.
  Unique comment/version prevents duplicate notices.
  Email failure never rolls back the decision or notice.
  Pending/approved author UI has no moderation notices.
  Deleting a photo or video cascades to comments and notices.
end note
@enduml
